From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] Direct3D 11 predication skips texture copies, clears and resolves

Conditional rendering does not discard transfers, deferred load op clears or
render pass resolves. While a predicate is set, texture to texture, texture to
buffer and buffer to texture copies, render target, depth stencil and view clears,
unordered access view clears and resolves run as draws, clears of attachments
and dispatches inside conditional rendering, keep the destination contents
instead of discarding them, and are no longer deferred. Operations without a
predicate are unchanged.
